  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "When the batch modify parser encounters an inline xml datastream that looks like:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "<a:element xmlns:a=\"urn:example:a\">",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "<b:subelement xmlns:b=\"urn:example:b\">",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "</b:subelement>",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "</a:element>",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "...the output it sends to Fedora is not well-formed.  In particular, the namespace declarations are moved to the root, but still present in the sub-elements, minus the attribute name, like so:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "<a:element xmlns:a=\"urn:example:a\" xmlns:b=\"urn:example:b\">",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "<b:subelement =\"urn:example:b\">",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "</b:subelement>",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "</a:element>",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Ideally, the output that the batch modify utility sends to Fedora should be exactly the XML that occurs within the xmlContent element.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "This was originally reported by Deborah Kaplan at Tufts on May 27th, 2008.  It was thought to have been fixed by bugfix #1838750, but on July 11th, Deborah reported that wasn't the case and I verified.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "A fix should ensure any well-formed inline XML, regardless of how namespaces are declared, arrives to Fedora in the same way it was given in the batch modify directives file – without changing where namespaces are declared.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "This bug needs to be fixed in trunk and maintenance-2.2, with appropriate tests.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
