     "body": "<p>The attached .jar files are fedora-client.jar replacements that fix this issue for Fedora 2.2.4 and 3.1, respectively.  To apply:</p>\n\n<p>1) Back up your existing fedora/client/fedora-client.jar file<br/>\n2) Download the appropriate jar and save it as fedora/client/fedora-client.jar (over the existing file)</p>\n\n<p>If you use a source distribution, you can find the relevant source code for the class that changed (BatchModifyParser) at:</p>\n\n<p>For applying to 2.2.4:<br/>\n<a href=\"http://fedora-commons.svn.sourceforge.net/viewvc/fedora-commons/fedora/branches/maintenance-2.2/src/java/fedora/client/batch/BatchModifyParser.java?revision=7910\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://fedora-commons.svn.sourceforge.net/viewvc/fedora-commons/fedora/branches/maintenance-2.2/src/java/fedora/client/batch/BatchModifyParser.java?revision=7910</a></p>\n\n<p>For applying to 3.1:<br/>\n<a href=\"http://fedora-commons.svn.sourceforge.net/viewvc/fedora-commons/fedora/trunk/src/java/fedora/client/batch/BatchModifyParser.java?revision=7902\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://fedora-commons.svn.sourceforge.net/viewvc/fedora-commons/fedora/trunk/src/java/fedora/client/batch/BatchModifyParser.java?revision=7902</a></p>",
     "created": "02/Feb/09 11:37 PM",
